reviews from training-data knowledge only.\" The `groundWithGoogleSearch: true` parameter is passed but has zero effect. The comment mentions a `GEMINI_API_KEY` escape valve for native Google API grounding that is \"not yet wired.\" This means R4's fact-check is entirely ungrounded — the PDF's §fact-check badge implies web verification that never happens.\n\n11. **(enrich-state-with-reference-anchor.tsx:batchLookup) `PYTHON_BIN` env var — SILENT FALLBACK TO `python3`.** If `python3` isn't on PATH (common on macOS post-Monterey where `python3` requires Xcode CLI tools), the spawn fails and the entire Engine C step throws, caught by the chain's try/catch which continues without reference anchoring. No error surfaces to the PDF reader — the cover's REF panel just shows no data.\n\n12. **(enrich-state-with-reference-anchor.tsx:FORGE_TRUTH_DB path) `~/.forge-truth/forge-truth.db` — MISSING DB SILENTLY DEGRADES.** Both Engine B (estimate-missing-prices.tsx via `CorpusClassifier`) and Engine C (via `reference_lookup.py`) depend on this SQLite database. If the DB file doesn't exist (fresh machine, no corpus build step run), Engine B falls back to 100% Flash-Lite classification (more expensive, less accurate) and Engine C's Python subprocess will fail on import. Neither case produces a user-visible error in the PDF.\n\n13. **(serial-design-chain-v2.tsx:env bootstrap) `~/.claude/secrets/tavily.env` — LOADED BUT NEVER CONSUMED.** The chain loads this env file at startup, but no stage in the chain actually calls the Tavily search API. The research synthesis stage (`runResearchSynthesis`) uses a different search provider. The Tavily key sits in memory unused; if it were removed, nothing would change.\n\n14. **(render-minimal-pdf.tsx:getClassStandards call) `getClassStandards(productClass)` — CLASS STANDARDS TABLE MAY HAVE INCOMPLETE COVERAGE.** The renderer calls `getClassStandards()` and `mergeBriefAndClassStandards()` to build the regulatory standards section. If the product c